h the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡n}{\\sqrt{n}}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges,  and its limit is $0.$" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269210 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269211 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269212 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269213 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269214 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1041 "selection" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1104 #edb/ref 17592186269213 13194139533964 true] [17592186269209 1110 #uuid "cdd70aae-b710-56ec-8da7-ca1d444dcc04" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269210 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533964 true] [17592186269210 1111 #uuid "85310aea-7c71-545d-ae67-ff8b406595cf" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269211 1034 "2" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533964 true] [17592186269211 1111 #uuid "fba6c2f6-ca67-5229-9783-246316e5a8c1" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269212 1034 "1" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533964 true] [17592186269212 1111 #uuid "b7e9c920-31a4-56fd-9909-3458a854c736" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269213 1034 "0" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533964 true] [17592186269213 1111 #uuid "e402331b-8062-58ed-a635-0c5944cae424" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269214 1034 "The sequence diverges" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533964 true] [17592186269214 1111 #uuid "a70d209b-f9f1-52b6-b581-1246b2d089f2" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186269216 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1089 "q-123709" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1100 "Does the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5n)}{{n}^{5}}-1$ for $n\\ge 1$ converge or diverge? If the sequence converges, what is its limit?" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1113 #uuid "7a376b33-d2ce-5d81-8804-ae92cf43873c" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269215 1145 "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5n)}{{n}^{5}}-1)=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5n)}{{n}^{5}}\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5n)}{{n}^{5}}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5n)}{{n}^{5}}=-1+0=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges and its limit is $-1.$" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269217 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269218 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269219 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269220 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269221 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1041 "selection" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1104 #edb/ref 17592186269220 13194139533964 true] [17592186269216 1110 #uuid "c05be86d-cad3-5604-9693-35234f2759f4" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269217 1034 "1" 13194139533964 true] [17592186269217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533964 true] [1759218